The bug is in the `pullFromCache` function that `GroupByQueryQueryToolChest.getCacheStrategy` builds, in the loop that restores post-aggregators from the result-level cache (`processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/groupby/GroupByQueryQueryToolChest.java:653-659`):

```java
Iterator<PostAggregator> postItr = query.getPostAggregatorSpecs().iterator();
int postPos = 0;
while (postItr.hasNext() && results.hasNext()) {
  resultRow.set(postAggregatorStart + postPos, results.next());
}
```

The loop never calls `postItr.next()` and never increments `postPos`. Every remaining cached value is therefore written to the first post-aggregator slot, each overwriting the one before.

This matches the issue's output. `a2` shows `a3`'s value (31,548) and `a3` is NULL. With zero or one post-aggregator, the loop happens to give the correct result.

The fix is to advance both inside the loop: call `postItr.next()` and do `postPos++`. `prepareForCache` writes the post-aggregators in order, so it doesn't appear to need a change. I found this by reading the code; I didn't run or edit anything.

